  "energy_arc": "Mukhada statement opens at high-octane mid-tempo heavy metal drive; Antara elevates intensity into the upper register; Taan unleashes maximum speed and technical fire at the climax; Final Mukhada delivers a devastating, authoritative unison resolution.",
  "rhythm_section": {
    "reasoning": "Plan: Ground the key in E (Sa) with heavy NWOBHM galloping power chords in Raga Bhairav. In Section 0 (mukhada), establish the recurring chord pattern: 8 beats of S, 4 beats of r, 2 beats of d, 2 beats of S, blending palm-muted chugs and open sustained power chords to let the sitar's ornamentation speak. In Section 1 (antara), move harmony through S (8 beats), m (4 beats), d (2 beats), and S (2 beats) while climbing into higher register voicing (+1) to lift with the sitar's upper register and provide ringing resonance. In Section 2 (taan_long), simplify the harmonic progression to an unrelenting driving pedal on S (12 beats) and r to S resolution (2 + 2 beats) with constant galloping 16th/8th palm mutes supporting the sitar's rapid chaugun taans. Section 3 (final mukhada) mirrors Section 0 via same_as for a unified, crushing recapitulation.",
